   "Northwind-negotiator": "competing",
   "Halcyon-researcher": "collaborating",
   "Halcyon-drafter": "competing",
   "Halcyon-negotiator": "competing"
  },
  "holistic_F_N": 1,
  "holistic_F_H": 2,
  "section_notes": "S1 is strict: all thermal incidents reported within 24h, final investigation within 30 days, and customer notice within 72h. S2 sets a 55°C test and 5% threshold but only triggers corrective action (no sales stop), with numeric failure rates disclosed to customers but not publicly. S3 requires new-unit shut-off immediately and installed-unit retrofit within 6 years; S4 requires built-in suppression at 36 months; S5 has no mandatory numeric recall, with 8/100k triggering regulator review and open-ended corrective action, and recall only for imminent serious risk."
 },
